Web Inspector, GTK: keep the data to save alive until the write has run.

Saving from the inspector (a console message, a resource) wrote a file that
began with heap garbage instead of the content.  platformSave() decoded or
UTF-8-encoded the content into two locals and handed their pointer to
g_file_replace_contents_async(), which takes no copy (it wraps the pointer
with g_bytes_new_static) and performs the write from a worker thread,
main-loop iterations later -- after platformSave() has returned and freed
the locals.  The write then read whatever the allocator had put into the
released memory.

Hold the data in a heap structure owned by the asynchronous operation and
release it in the completion callback, which is what the upstream
refactoring of this code (WebInspectorUIProxyGLib.cpp) does today.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Inspector/gtk/WebInspectorUIProxyGtk.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Inspector/gtk/WebInspectorUIProxyGtk.cpp
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@
